WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.436 --> 00:00:03.586
Unit twenty-three. Sprains and Strains!

2
00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:08.052
Hello, everyone! I'm Doctor Visal, your school doctor.

3
00:00:08.102 --> 00:00:11.290
Hi, Doctor Visal! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:15.058
Today we learn about Sprains and Strains. Let's go!

5
00:00:16.273 --> 00:00:19.540
Sprain. Say it with me. Sprain!

6
00:00:23.058 --> 00:00:25.992
Strain. Say it with me. Strain!

7
00:00:29.493 --> 00:00:32.610
Ligament. Say it with me. Ligament!

8
00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:39.236
Muscle. Say it with me. Muscle!

9
00:00:42.744 --> 00:00:46.161
Swelling. Say it with me. Swelling!

10
00:00:49.631 --> 00:00:52.848
Rest. Say it with me. Rest!

11
00:00:56.387 --> 00:00:59.671
Ice. Say it with me. Ice!

12
00:01:03.152 --> 00:01:05.952
Doctor. Say it with me. Doctor!

13
00:01:09.466 --> 00:01:17.862
A sprain injures a ligament; a strain injures a muscle. Swelling and pain are common. Rest, a wrapped ice pack, and seeing a doctor for severe injuries help recovery.

14
00:01:17.912 --> 00:01:20.519
Now I understand. Thank you, Doctor Visal!

15
00:01:22.097 --> 00:01:27.105
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:27.154 --> 00:01:28.305
Ligament!

17
00:01:29.201 --> 00:01:34.294
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:34.344 --> 00:01:35.494
Ice!

19
00:01:36.401 --> 00:01:42.552
Did you know? Ice should always be wrapped in a cloth — never put it directly on skin!

20
00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.550
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:45.245 --> 00:01:53.440
Think and answer. What is the difference between a sprain and a strain?

22
00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:54.640
Great answer!

23
00:01:55.664 --> 00:02:00.651
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:00.701 --> 00:02:03.376
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

